      },
      "message": "fix(evidence): serialize concurrent C19 long-run records on directory inode\n\nWHY: Independent sample/run/checkpoint/stop processes previously read the same\nlast sequence and could write duplicate or post-seal records despite individually\nfsynced appends. A passing 7/30-day wall-clock report must not depend on a\nsingle-writer scheduling assumption.\n\nUse Linux directory flock for atomic read/check/append and terminal stop, with\nshared report reads (exclusive when publishing a report), no replaceable\nsidecar file, and fail-closed directory replacement detection. Preserve the\nschema, raw bytes, existing gap/Unknown admission and wall-clock obligations.\nAdd two real subprocess concurrency regressions, retaining 15 original cases.\n\nEvidence: code/static review and local Linux flock probe only; exact branch\nCI and multi-day evidence remain required.",
